* sg13g2-bandgap -- closed-loop AC output-impedance-at-vref PEX bench body for the `klt sim`
* harness (issue #278, the remaining half of #275). Instantiated by
* sim/closed-loop-zout-pex/run_klt_sim.sh, which substitutes @@OSDI_DIR@@,
* @@VDD@@, the four @@*_SEED@@ nodeset values (sim/closed-loop-startup's
* newest committed record, 125 C row for this process corner and supply
* -- the worst-corner stiffness; the fs/125 point singular-matrixed from
* the 27 C row on the refreshed extraction -- while the op-match check
* uses the per-temperature reference via --seed-csv) and @@PEX_BODY@@. The
* DUT half is GENERATED by `sim/tools/gen_pex_netlist_body.py --cell top`.
*
* `klt sim` netlist-body convention: this file is a circuit BODY. No
* `.lib`, no `.temp`, no `.options temp=`, no analysis card, no `.end`.
*
* WHY NODESET-SEEDED, NOT RAMP-SETTLED. The transient benches in this
* issue settle by ramping vdd 0->VDD and measuring the tail; this bench
* tried the same shape first and it DOES NOT TRANSFER: ngspice re-solves
* the DC operating point for an `ac` analysis from the sources' DC values
* -- a PWL source's DC value is its t=0 point (0 V), so the AC
* linearisation lands on a collapsed supply, not the settled equilibrium
* (verified on ngspice 46 with a nonlinear toy circuit; a linear one
* cannot distinguish the two -- the trap that hid this initially). The
* seeds below are therefore the old bench's own mechanism, kept: they are
* convergence AIDS, not constraints -- the op they seed is checked in the
* enrichment pass against this body's own .nodeset values with the old
* bench's 50 mV tolerance.
*
* TWO DELIBERATE DEVIATIONS, both disclosed in sim/harness/README.md
* "Upstream friction":
*
* 1. The `.control` pre_osdi block (klayout-tools#2666) -- same as every
*    `klt sim` body in this repo.
* 2. The `.control` block also carries the seeded `op`, the op prints and
*    the AC sweep: the request schema declares ONE analysis and a bench
*    that must print its operating points needs them log-side
*    (`measurements[].expr`, the 0.6.0 answer, postdates the runner
*    image's klt 0.5.0). The request's declared analysis is the same
*    `ac dec 30 1 1e9`; `.nodeset` cards are parse-time, so klt's own
*    re-run of the analysis lands on the same seeded op, and the
*    top-level `.meas ac` cards attach to it. The body's `print psrr_db`
*    table lands in the per-corner log, which
*    sim/harness/enrich_ac_report.py parses for the curve-extremum
*    columns (worst-case PSRR and its frequency -- not expressible as a
*    0.5.0 `.meas` at all).
.control
pre_osdi @@OSDI_DIR@@/psp103.osdi
pre_osdi @@OSDI_DIR@@/psp103_nqs.osdi
pre_osdi @@OSDI_DIR@@/mosvar.osdi
pre_osdi @@OSDI_DIR@@/r3_cmc.osdi
op
print v(fb)
print v(sns1)
print v(sns2)
print v(vref)
print v(det)
print i(Vmkfb)
ac dec 30 1 1e9
let zout_db = db(v(vref))
print zout_db
.endc

* Node seeds: sim/closed-loop-startup's committed per-corner DC-bias
* values (125 C row for this process corner and supply -- the
* worst-corner stiffness; see the header), from the same record
* sim/lib/nodeset_seed.sh established as the hand-transcribed bench's
* seed provenance. Checked, not trusted: the enrichment pass verifies
* the landed op against that record's per-temperature reference with
* the old bench's 50 mV tolerance.
.nodeset v(fb)=@@FB_SEED@@ v(sns1)=@@SNS1_SEED@@ v(sns2)=@@SNS2_SEED@@ v(vref)=@@VREF_SEED@@

* Solver options: reltol=5e-3 (settled trim-bearing setting); rshunt/gmin
* deliberately absent (issue #278 -- ~0.55 uA ladder leak, ~37 mV vref
* artifact).
.options reltol=5e-3

* Resident-vector save (issue #278 work item 3): every vector the op
* prints, the meas cards and the print table read; nothing else resident.
.save v(fb) v(sns1) v(sns2) v(vref) v(det) i(Vmkfb)

* FIXTURE -- supply: a plain DC source, carrying NO AC term here. This
* experiment perturbs a completely different port: Itest injects the
* 1 A / 0 deg AC test current directly at vref (DC = 0, so it does not
* perturb the seeded DC operating point), and Zout = db(v(vref)) for a
* 1 A stimulus -- the injection method this experiment's README
* documents. @@VDD@@ is substituted per supply by the runner (the seed
* set is per-supply too, so the supply axis lives in per-supply body
* variants, not in the request's `alter` channel).
Vvdd vdd 0 DC @@VDD@@
Vvss vss 0 dc 0

* STIMULUS -- the 1 A / 0 deg AC test current at vref.
Itest 0 vref DC 0 AC 1 0

* FIXTURE -- vsubs is tied to vss through a 0 V source, NOT through the
* 1 TOhm DC tie the extraction itself carries (which remains in parallel,
* harmlessly): at AC a 1 TOhm return leaves vsubs effectively floating,
* and every extracted ground capacitance stops being a cap to ground and
* instead couples net-to-net in series with the other nets' ground caps --
* which is not what the layout does. In this bench the far plate IS the
* substrate and the substrate is tied to vss. The measured size of that
* choice is quantified, not asserted, in this experiment's README ("The
* vsubs tie matters here").
Vsubs_tie vsubs vss dc 0

* DUT -- generated PEX body for bandgap_top (Vmkfb split included, for
* topology parity with every other closed-loop bench; its current is not
* probed here -- this bench's measurement is the AC curve at vref).
.include @@PEX_BODY@@
